    "text": "<h2>Summary</h2>\n\n<ul>\n\t<li>A <code>String</code> consists of a series of characters, and we represent Strings by placing these characters in between double-quotes.</li>\n\t<li>We can append two <code>String</code>s by using the <code>+</code> operator.</li>\n\t<li>If we want to represent non-integer numbers in Java, we can do this using a <code>double</code>. However, a <code>double</code> can only represent an approximation of a number and may not be entirely precise.</li>\n\t<li><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dorothy_Vaughan\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\">Dorothy Vaughan</a>, mathematician and human computer at NACA</li>\n\t<li><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ada_Lovelace\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\">Ada Lovelace</a>, “Grandmother of Computing”</li>\n</ul>",
